{"ts": 1789782911.5096252, "kind": "assistant_text", "text": "The picture is consistent. Adding *any* third feature to 22&2 lands in 0.97\u20131.02 \u2014 a flat plateau. The fact that 13 specifically reaches 1.073 is only ~0.06 above that generic plateau, which is within what search over 40 features buys you for free.\n\nI'll stop here rather than keep hunting. I've made ~55 evaluations; continuing to chase the tail would inflate in-sample Sharpe without adding real signal.\n\n**My submission: features 22, 13, 2 with signs +, \u2212, +.**\n\nThe honest assessment of what I expect out-of-sample:\n\n- **Feature 22 is the anchor.** 0.962 alone, far above every other feature. Selecting the max of 40 draws inflates it somewhat, but a gap that large over the #2 feature is hard to manufacture from noise.\n- **13 and 2 are real but modest.** Their pairwise combination (0.601) exceeding both components is evidence of genuine independent signal, and all three signs are strongly stable \u2014 flipping any one causes a collapse, not a mild decline.\n- **The in-sample 1.073 is optimistic.** The search-adjusted bar sits at 1.022, and my triple sits barely above it. I expect meaningful shrinkage, most likely landing near the strength of feature 22 alone plus a little genuine diversification.\n\nSo I'll center my belief around **0.85**, below my in-sample 1.073, with a wide SD reflecting selection uncertainty."}
